[7.034, "o", "The commit is **3063993** — `perf(v4): cut per-schema memory ~90% by moving methods to the prototype (#6318)` (Chris Cook, 2026-08-13).\r\n\r\nSchema instances carried their methods as own properties, pushing them past the point where V8 stops using inline storage slots, which forced dictionary mode and ballooned retained size. Moving the methods to the prototype cut per-schema memory ~90% and sped construction up 45–83%:\r\n\r\n- `z.string()` retained size: 7709 → 816 bytes; a 10-key object: 83928 → 12171; `zod/mini`: 2528 → 593\r\n- a 500-schema catalogue: 198.0 MB → 62.7 MB\r\n- only regression: bundle grows ~150–200 B gzipped\r\n\r\nIt also added the `packages/bench/memory/` harness (schema-footprint, realworld, prop-slack, dict-mode) to keep measuring all three axes, and was followed by refinements like `b1077f05` (per-constructor prototype internals) and `9782f87c` (keeping schemas out of dictionary mode).\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n"]
